      "titre": "File:Light & Air - Ceiling fan with light, Mid-City New Orleans.jpg",
      "description": "October 30th, 2004: My big project for today was installing a new ceiling fan in our bedroom. First I had to buy one. Instead of going out to a Home Depot in the suburbs, I went to Armstrong’s which is only a few blocks from our house in Mid-City. I had to wait my turn, but it was well worth it, because the saleslady was very helpful. The ceiling fans weren’t just off-the-shelf kits; you had to build your own. I couldn’t have put together all the components without some assistance. I ended up taking home a Craftmade Phoenix PX52 with a brushed nickel finish, oak blades, a four bulb lamp and so",
